 to v5.0.0.\n2. Roll back only `payments-worker` to v3.3.0.\n3. Roll back both.\n\nBoth target versions were healthy in production before, so no change-manager approval is needed. Once you tell me which service or services, I'll open a SEV2 for each one I roll back.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0114X8oCNKoULEDhdcgW1VCo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014sMh5xW5oBa8hoLmnNfYEy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) was unhealthy in all production regions with an 18% error rate, which caused errors further down in payments-api (v5.1.0, degraded, 18% error rate). Rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last healthy release, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Next steps: confirm payments-worker and payments-api recover, and find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R9KJzrfUnp5U4zsZzkxGXm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GWkX3XtTub7XFERAtyBRDs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and it's healthy again. payments-api is still failing, though.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It went to an approver automatically and was approved. A fresh status check shows it healthy, with errors down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 **INC-0001** for payments-worker, which paged on-call. The summary covers the bad v3.4.0 deploy, the rollback, and the effect on payments-api. I set a fixed key on the request so a retry can't open a duplicate incident or page again.\n- **Still open:** payments-api (v5.1.0) is still degraded at an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. But its v5.1.0 deploy is also marked degraded, so it could have a problem of its own. I haven't touched it.\n\nI'd check payments-api again in a few minutes. If it hasn't recovered, I can roll it back to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release, so no change-manager approval needed) and add that to INC-0001. Do you want me to?", "type": "text"}]}]}